<%# locals: id, messages -- the Turbo Stream replacement target for one
    autosaving field's error slot (cs-studio spec §6.1). Rendered with the
    same markup every `Admin::Columns::*` component already builds inline
    (matching classes, same "wrap every message in its own <p>" shape) so a
    field looks identical whether its errors came from the initial page
    load or a later autosave replace -- and always rendered, even with an
    empty `messages`, since an empty replace is exactly what clears a
    field's stale error once the value that caused it is fixed
    (`Admin::AutosaveResponses#autosave_stream`). %>
<div id="<%= id %>" class="mt-1 text-sm text-danger-ink">
  <% messages.each do |message| %>
    <p><%= message %></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
